    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0092" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg82"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 574.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 14, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have prepared a note to Lord Russell,
                    based on the instructions contained in your despatch, No. 789, and the copy of
                    the whole report of Mr. Mallory, which has been received here as printed in the
                    New York Times of the 30th December. But on a close examination of this paper so
                    much of it seemed to justify a suspicion of its entire genuineness that I have
                    concluded to defer sending it at least until after the receipt of further
                    intelligence from America. It is not unlikely that some further notice of the
                    report, after it shall have reached you in its full extent, may accompany the
                    copy you expressed an intention to transmit when obtained.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. H. Seward</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
